9+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiigFBVV95cUxPZzJsWlBSWDZydDBadXQ5Vnl2VEhjSHdJSElwUkNTQV8zZ2xmWGNCVWh0WUprX1pQZDNsZExOeFpsMUZ2Tk1od1ZlZFAtTDduVDY0UV9fWXRfcjBHeS1jOXo0ZjFZdXlmbkFyYWRoWkFSbDduSnJhak1DTDBQUXpJdXNpUTZvYXAzZUE?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 3.65, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 4.0, "poll_sd": 5.65, "poll_weight": 0.47, "fundamentals": {"margin": 3.23, "lean": 0.0, "environment": 4.45, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.22}, "rating_margin": 3.94, "sigma_race": 5.0, "sigma_total": 5.42, "baseline_margin": 3.82, "analyst_adjustment": 0.68, "key_factors": ["Consistent polling lead for Crowley, including a 7-point final Marquette survey", "Prediction markets price Crowley at roughly 82-84% to win", "Tiffany's large fundraising edge partially offsets the polling deficit", "Open seat with no incumbent on the ballot in an even-PVI state"], "rationale": "Polling averages put Crowley up about 4-5 points, expert ratings mostly call it Lean D, and markets price him near 82-84%, all pointing to a modest but real Democratic edge. Tiffany's fundraising advantage keeps this from reaching Likely D.", "watch": "A late shift toward Tiffany, or polling error in either direction in a state with a history of razor-thin margins, could move this into Tossup or Likely D territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tony Evers (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin's governorship is open with Tony Evers retiring, and Milwaukee County executive David Crowley faces congressman Tom Tiffany. Polling across the fall has consistently shown Crowley ahead, with the final Marquette University survey giving him a 51-44 lead and averages clustering around a 4-5 point margin. Expert ratings lean Democratic, though Fox News and RealClearPolitics call it a Tossup, and prediction markets price Crowley's chances in the low-to-mid 80s.\n\nTiffany has a clear money advantage, raising over $10 million to Crowley's roughly $1 million, which keep